    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Step 1:  To determine the number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles, we need to consider the different combinations he can make with the seven marbles at hand.\nStep 2:  When selecting three marbles from seven, order does not matter. Therefore, the problem can be diagonalized into a combination counting problem using the combination formula.\n\nStep 3:  The formula for combination is given by nCr = n! / r!(n – r)!, where n represents the total number of items (in this case, marbles), and r represents the size of the group we are selecting (here, three different marbles).\nStep 4:  Applying this formula to our problem, we have n = 7 marbles and r = 3 marbles.\nStep 5:  Therefore, we need to calculate nCr = 7! / 3!(7 – 3)!, which equals (7 * 6 * 5) divided by (3 * 2 * 1).\n\nStep 6:  By applying this methodology, we can find the total number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag to play the game. The final approach instructs to plug other values into the alternative formula nCr = n! / r!(n – r)!.\n```python\nimport math\n\nnum_marbles = 7\nmarble_groups = 3\n\nnum_ways = math.factorial(num_marbles) / (math.factorial(marble_groups) * math.factorial(num_marbles - marble_groups))\nprint(num_ways)\n```\n\nThe output of the program will give the final answer for the number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag of seven.",
