      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We can solve this problem using the formula for combinations. The formula for combinations is given by:\nCombinations = n! / r! (n-r)! \nwhere n is the total number of items, r is the number of items to be chosen, and ! denotes the factorial of a number. In this case, Johnny has 7 different colored marbles, so n = 7, and he wants to choose 3 marbles, so r = 3.\nCombinations = 7! / 3! (7-3)! \n= 7! / 3! 4! \n= (7 * 6 * 5 * 4 * 3 * 2 * 1) / (3 * 2 * 1) * (4 * 3 * 2 * 1) \n= (7 * 6 * 5) / (1 * 1 * 1 * 2 * 3 * 4) \n= (7 * 6 * 5) / (1 * 1 * 2 * 3) \n= 35\nSo Johnny can choose three different marbles from his bag in 35 different ways.\nThe answer is: 35",
